---
/*
  /lab/attio/ — the Attio surface in the palette comparison set.

  One surface (near-white ground, near-neutral cool greys, a single teal-green
  accent), seven fixed blocks (K1–K7 from lab-editing-map.md §6), painted in
  Attio's tokens and sequenced in Attio's order: K2 K4 K1 K5 K3 K7 K6.

  Attio's signature is the "carved / precise" look: 1px *inner* borders on cards
  and inputs (box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule)), a modest 8px card radius,
  and a single teal accent doing all the work on an otherwise all-neutral field.
  Data-dense but airy. The carved borders are leaned into on K2 (the Linear
  rhythm list) and K4 (the Stripe dense block), whose grids suit them.

  No serif here — the neutral body face is Roboto Flex throughout, per the K
  definitions. Gradients kept to a whisper (Attio is crisp/white): only K7 the
  statement close takes a focal shift; the carved borders + single teal carry
  the rest.

  Own shell — no BaseLayout. Static. Content verbatim from technical-editing.md §5.
*/
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>/lab/attio — near-white carved surface</title>
  <meta
    name="description"
    content="The Attio surface: near-white ground, near-neutral greys, a single teal accent, 1px carved inner borders, modest radius. Seven fixed editing blocks in Attio's order."
  />

  <!-- Fonts via Google Fonts. The six originals. -->
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cuprum:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400;1,700&family=Nova+Square&family=Oxanium:wght@400;600;700&family=Roboto+Flex:opsz,wght@8..144,300;8..144,400;8..144,600&family=Space+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Ubuntu+Condensed&display=swap"
    rel="stylesheet"
  />

  <style is:global>
    :root {
      /* Attio surface tokens (editing-choices-directory.md PART A) */
      --surface: #FFFFFF;        /* near-white ground */
      --surface-lift: #FFFFFF;   /* peripheral / receding — Attio stays white */
      --surface-deep: #F0F2F3;   /* ~6% toward a cool near-black — focal only */
      --surface-2: #F7F8F9;      /* near-neutral grey secondary ground */
      --ink: #17191C;            /* cool near-black */
      --ink-soft: rgba(23, 25, 28, 0.64);
      --ink-mute: rgba(23, 25, 28, 0.54);
      --accent: #0E7C66;         /* single teal-green accent */
      --accent-deep: #0A6352;
      --rule: #E3E6E8;           /* crisp 1px carved rule (cards + inputs) */
      --rule-soft: rgba(23, 25, 28, 0.08); /* lighter separator within lists */
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--surface);
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: 'Roboto Flex', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.65;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
    }

    .page { display: block; }

    /* One block = one editing treatment. Airy padding on an all-neutral field. */
    .blk { padding: 5rem 1.5rem; }
    .blk--2 { background: var(--surface-2); }

    .col { max-width: 62ch; margin-inline: auto; }

    /* Soft focus-directing gradient (technical-editing.md §3), delta ≤ ~6% — a whisper.
       Attio is crisp/white, so only the focal close uses one. */
    .grad-focus { background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--surface) 0%, var(--surface-deep) 100%); }

    /* The carved look: 1px inner border, never an outer stroke. Modest 8px radius. */
    .carved {
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule);
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: var(--surface);
    }

    /* Captions: italic, muted, in the block's own font, ≤16. */
    .cap { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-mute); margin-top: 1.75rem; }
    .cap em { font-style: italic; }

    .note { font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink-soft); }

    a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
    a:hover { color: var(--accent-deep); }

    .r8 { border-radius: 8px; }

    /* ---- K2 rhythm list (Ubuntu Condensed head + Roboto Flex items) — Linear ----
       Leaned-in carved card: the whole list sits in a 1px inner border, items
       separated by hairline rules. Attio's tight grid, rendered. */
    .k2-eyebrow {
      font-family: 'Roboto Flex', sans-serif;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.4px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--accent);
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }
    .k2-head {
      font-family: 'Ubuntu Condensed', sans-serif;
      font-size: 32px;
      line-height: 1.15;
      letter-spacing: -0.022em;
      margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    }
    .k2-list { list-style: none; padding: 0.25rem 1.5rem; margin: 0; }
    .k2-list li {
      font-family: 'Roboto Flex', sans-serif;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      padding-block: 1rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
    }
    .k2-list li:first-child { border-top: none; }
    .k2-list li b { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); }

    /* ---- K4 stat-dense (Space Mono figure + source/caveat) — Stripe ----
       Each stat is its own carved card: the dense block reads light because the
       1px inner border gives every figure a precise seat. */
    .k4-eyebrow {
      font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 14px;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .k4-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
    .stat { padding: 1.35rem 1.5rem; }
    .fig {
      font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 28px;
      line-height: 1.2;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--accent);
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    }
    .src { font-family: 'Roboto Flex', sans-serif; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }

    /* ---- K1 premise (prose) — Stripe Press ---- */
    .k1-eyebrow {
      font-family: 'Roboto Flex', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 14px;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--accent);
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    .k1-body { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }

    /* ---- K5 bare frame (Oxanium head + neutral body + mono doc-excerpt) — Stripe ---- */
    .k5-head {
      font-family: 'Oxanium', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 28px;
      line-height: 1.2;
      margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    }
    .k5-body { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1.75rem; }
    .bare { margin: 0; }
    .doc-excerpt {
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      background: var(--surface);
      font-family: 'Space Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
    .doc-excerpt .anno { color: var(--accent); }
    figcaption { margin-top: 1rem; }

    /* ---- K3 long-text list (Cuprum head + neutral reading) + plain CTA — 37signals ---- */
    .k3-head {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 30px;
      line-height: 1.2;
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .k3-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 2rem; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; }
    .k3-list li { margin: 0 0 1.15rem; }
    .k3-list b { font-weight: 600; }
    .cta { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
    .btn {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: 'Roboto Flex', sans-serif;
      font-size: 18px;
      font-weight: 600;
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #FFFFFF;
      padding: 0.7rem 1.35rem;
      border-radius: 8px;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .btn:hover { background: var(--accent-deep); color: #FFFFFF; }

    /* ---- K7 statement close (Nova Square + Roboto Flex) ---- */
    .k7-head {
      font-family: 'Nova Square', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-size: 36px;
      line-height: 1.15;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    }
    .k7-body { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
    .k7-body + .k7-body { margin-top: 1rem; }

    /* ---- K6 sidenote (Cuprum italic head + neutral body + margin note) — Works in Progress ---- */
    .k6-head {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-style: italic;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 28px;
      line-height: 1.2;
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .k6-wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 62ch) 15rem; gap: 2.5rem; align-items: start; }
    .k6-body { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
    .k6-side {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-style: italic;
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      padding-top: 0.4rem;
    }
    @media (max-width: 820px) {
      .k6-wrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .k6-side { border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 1rem; }
    }

    /* Per-block caption fonts (each caption in its own block's font). */
    .k2-cap { font-family: 'Ubuntu Condensed', sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.01em; }
    .k4-cap { font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace; }
    .k1-cap, .k7-cap { font-family: 'Roboto Flex', sans-serif; }
    .k5-cap { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
    .k3-cap, .k6-cap { font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif; }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <main class="page">

    <!-- ============ K2 — palette + surface (rhythm list) ============ -->
    <!-- template: rhythm-list · treatment: Linear -->
    <section class="blk">
      <div class="col">
        <p class="k2-eyebrow">Palette + surface</p>
        <h1 class="k2-head">The white-main systems worth copying wholesale</h1>
        <ul class="k2-list carved">
          <li><b>Mercury</b> — the reference for premium-restrained off-white. Near-invisible borders, almost no shadow, one accent used sparingly. Serious without being cold, which is your construction-buyer problem exactly.</li>
          <li><b>Anthropic</b> — warm ivory ground, serif headings, very low saturation. Closest live example of your §1 brief: calm enough to read as a default rather than a pitch.</li>
          <li><b>Attio</b> — white, precise, tight grid. Shows how far a single accent goes when everything else is neutral.</li>
          <li><b>Notion</b> — the smoothed-edges reference. Radius scale, soft card fills, warm white. Study it for where rounding stops; over-rounding is what makes a premium site read as a toy.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="cap k2-cap"><em>Ubuntu Condensed head 32 (−.022em) + Roboto Flex items 18/1.6, tracked teal eyebrow +.4px · 62ch · left · 1px carved inner border (inset), hairline rules between items · r8 · 5rem:1rem — similar to Linear.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ K4 — block rhythm and sequencing (stat-dense) ============ -->
    <!-- template: stat-dense · treatment: Stripe -->
    <section class="blk blk--2">
      <div class="col">
        <p class="k4-eyebrow">// block rhythm and sequencing — big SaaS</p>
        <div class="k4-grid">
          <div class="stat carved">
            <div class="fig">Linear</div>
            <p class="src">take the spacing rhythm and the restraint, invert the palette. The lesson is vertical rhythm, and whitespace used structurally.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stat carved">
            <div class="fig">Stripe</div>
            <p class="src">how to sequence dense information so density stops feeling heavy. Useful for your §5, where you have a statistic plus a source plus a caveat in one block.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="cap k4-cap"><em>Space Mono figure 28 (teal) + Roboto Flex source 18, eyebrow 14 note · 62ch · left · each stat a 1px carved inner-border card (inset) · r8 · 5rem:1rem — similar to Stripe.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ K1 — premise (prose) ============ -->
    <!-- template: prose · treatment: Stripe Press -->
    <section class="blk">
      <div class="col">
        <p class="k1-eyebrow">Premise</p>
        <p class="k1-body">Your premise holds. A live site is a better template source than a template marketplace, because you can read the decisions rather than inherit someone's content model. And the reskin is only about six variables: neutral ramp, one accent, radius scale, spacing scale, text measure, border weight. Fix those six and any layout you admire becomes yours.</p>
        <p class="cap k1-cap"><em>Roboto Flex teal eyebrow + Roboto Flex body 18/1.65 · 62ch · left · no border (bare prose) · r8 tokens · 5rem:0 — similar to Stripe Press.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ K5 — bare imagery (bare frame / doc-excerpt) ============ -->
    <!-- template: bare-frame · treatment: Stripe -->
    <section class="blk blk--2">
      <div class="col">
        <h2 class="k5-head">Bare imagery</h2>
        <p class="k5-body">Mercury, Ramp, and Arc all show images without device frames, drop shadows, or perspective tilt. That is the current premium signal, and it happens to be the only image treatment that fits you.</p>
        <figure class="bare">
          <div class="doc-excerpt"><span class="anno"># teardown — annotation layer</span>
&gt; hero      no device frame · no shadow · no tilt
&gt; measure   62ch
&gt; radius    8px
&gt; border    1px inner (carved)
<span class="anno">&gt; note      the artifact IS the image</span></div>
          <figcaption class="note">Bare frame stands in for the image: a monospace document excerpt, no chrome.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="cap k5-cap"><em>Oxanium head 28 + Roboto Flex body 18/1.6 + Space Mono doc-excerpt 16 · 62ch · left · 1px carved inner frame (inset) · r8 · 5rem:1.75rem — similar to Stripe.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ K3 — long-text handling (list) + CTA ============ -->
    <!-- template: prose-list · treatment: 37signals/Basecamp -->
    <section class="blk">
      <div class="col">
        <h2 class="k3-head">Long-text handling</h2>
        <ul class="k3-list">
          <li><b>Stripe Press</b> — book typography on the web. Measure control, no chrome, headings that hold their own without decoration.</li>
          <li><b>Works in Progress</b> — sidenotes, footnotes, sustained reading. Relevant to your Notion-docs layer and the sample teardowns.</li>
          <li><b>37signals / Basecamp</b> — plain speech, opinionated blocks, one CTA, active refusal of decoration. The nearest ethos match to your §6 and §9.</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- template: plain-cta · treatment: Basecamp -->
        <div class="cta">
          <a class="btn" href="/varpage/teardown/">Request a free teardown &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <p class="cap k3-cap"><em>Cuprum head 30 + Roboto Flex reading 18/1.6, one teal CTA · 62ch · left · no border (plain speech) · r8 button · 5rem:1.15rem — similar to 37signals / Basecamp.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ K7 — harvest close (statement) ============ -->
    <!-- template: statement · treatment: Stripe Press -->
    <section class="blk grad-focus">
      <div class="col">
        <h2 class="k7-head">Five numbers and two fonts.</h2>
        <p class="k7-body">Open each of these, then write down only: the radius value, the body measure in characters, the border color and weight, the ratio between section padding and paragraph spacing, the type pairing. Five numbers and two fonts.</p>
        <p class="k7-body">That set, applied to any block library, gets you closer to a coherent site than any theme purchase will.</p>
        <p class="cap k7-cap"><em>Nova Square head 36 + Roboto Flex 18/1.65 · 62ch · left · no border · r8 tokens · focal grad (≤6%, white→cool) · 5rem:1rem — similar to Stripe Press.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ K6 — the 2026 warning (sidenote) ============ -->
    <!-- template: sidenote · treatment: Works in Progress -->
    <section class="blk blk--2">
      <div class="col" style="max-width: 82ch;">
        <h2 class="k6-head">One warning about the 2026 consensus</h2>
        <div class="k6-wrap">
          <div>
            <p class="k6-body">Every roundup this year says the same three things: put the product in motion at the top, add micro-interactions, consider dark mode. Two of those are wrong for you. You have no product UI to demo, and dark mode fights the calm-default frame you decided to install. Your equivalent of the interactive product moment is a real teardown excerpt rendered as a document — styled like a page from the artifact the client would receive, monospace annotations and all.</p>
          </div>
          <aside class="k6-side">That is your hero image and your §7 proof in one object.</aside>
        </div>
        <p class="cap k6-cap"><em>Cuprum italic head 28 + Roboto Flex body 18/1.6 · 62ch main + 15rem margin note (Cuprum italic 16) · no border · r8 tokens · 5rem:1.15rem — similar to Works in Progress.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</body>
</html>
